<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-14058] Create tests for large number of MDTs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14058</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/37759" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/37759&lt;/a&gt; "&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12506" title="Client unable to mount filesystem with very large number of MDTs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12506"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12506&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; changelog: support large number of MDT" allows clients to mount file systems with large numbers of MDTs. We need to create a, probably conf-sanity, test(s) that creates file systems with 16 and 32 MDTs and confirms that a client can mount this file system. The basic mount is a required test. Other testing with a large number of MDTs should be listed in this ticket.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
